[size=5][b]Valheim Builder Planner[/b][/size]
[i]Plan your builds outside the game, then rebuild them in your world — 100 % vanilla.[/i]

[b]Not a mod:[/b] a separate program for Windows. Your game, your saves and your achievements are not touched.
[b]No game files included:[/b] on first launch the planner reads the building pieces from [b]your own[/b] Valheim installation (about a minute), on your computer.

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every Hammer piece[/b] (around 390) with its real shape, size, cost and crafting station — names in the game's 36 languages
[*][b]Snapping like in the game[/b]: same snap points and rules, rotation in 22.5° steps, manual snap point choice
[*][b]Stability with the game's rules[/b] (wood, core wood, stone, iron, marble, ashstone…): blue → green → red, and a warning when something would collapse. The preview tells you before you place a piece.
[*][b]Floor view[/b]: top-down plan floor by floor, with the pieces and materials of each floor
[*][b]Rebuild guide[/b]: the plan in build order (floors → poles → walls → doors → beams → roof → furniture), the current step glows in 3D. Go back and forth freely.
[*][b]Materials list[/b] and a [b]build list export[/b] (checklist to keep on a second screen)
[*]Copy/paste, undo, autosave, save/open plans, Valheim-style flying camera
[*]Norse-style interface with piece thumbnails
[/list]

[size=4][b]Optional: PlanBuild[/b][/size]
For players who use the [b]PlanBuild[/b] mod: [i]Export ▾ → PlanBuild blueprint[/i] sends your plan to PlanBuild in one click (manual install, r2modman and Thunderstore profiles are detected). In game, the Blueprint Rune places it as ghost pieces to build with your materials.
You can also [b]open PlanBuild (.blueprint) and BuildShare (.vbuild) files[/b] from the community: check the cost and stability, then rebuild them vanilla with the guide.
[color=#e0b85a]Note: while any mod is loaded, Valheim disables achievements (nothing is saved to your character or world: without mods they work again). The planner itself needs no mod.[/color]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download and unzip anywhere (keep the folder together).
[*]Run [b]ValheimBuilderPlanner.exe[/b] (Windows 10/11, 64-bit).
[*]Click [b]Read my game[/b]. Valheim is found through Steam automatically, or choose its folder.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Controls[/b][/size]
Tab: menu / mouse · Mouse: look · WASD (ZQSD on AZERTY): fly · Space/C: up/down · Left click: place · Wheel or R: rotate · Middle click: remove · Shift+middle click: pick a piece · Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V: copy/paste · Ctrl+Z: undo · P: floor view · V: stability · B: guide

[size=4][b]Languages[/b][/size]
Piece names follow the game (36 languages). Interface: English and French — translations welcome on GitHub.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/ICCUser/valheim-builder-planner]github.com/ICCUser/valheim-builder-planner[/url]

